{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"A qualifying **in-kind ETF**—one meeting redemptions in securities/assets other than a de minimis amount of cash and publishing holdings daily—remains subject to:\n\n- A written liquidity-risk management program, including assessment, management and at-least-annual review of liquidity risk, with ETF-specific considerations.\n- The **15% of net assets limit on illiquid investments**, including identifying and monitoring illiquid holdings and applicable breach reporting and remediation.\n- Board oversight, designation of a program administrator, annual board reporting and recordkeeping.\n\nIt receives relief from:\n\n- Classifying every portfolio investment into the rule’s **four liquidity buckets**.\n- Establishing a **highly liquid investment minimum**, including the associated minimum-shortfall procedures and reporting.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Exemption from four-bucket classification is not exemption from identifying illiquid investments or complying with the 15% limit."}}
